  m_Name: RefrigeratorData
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  engineName: 'Refrigerator '
  engineDescription: A Refrigerator is a cooling system that removes heat from an
    enclosed space and rejects it to the surrounding environment using a vapour-compression
    refrigeration cycle. Its major components include the compressor, condenser,
    expansion device, evaporator, refrigerant, thermostat, and insulated cabinet.
    During operation, the compressor draws low-pressure refrigerant vapour from the
    evaporator and compresses it to a high pressure and temperature. The refrigerant
    then passes through the condenser, where it releases heat to the surroundings
    and changes into a high-pressure liquid. It flows through the expansion device,
    where its pressure and temperature decrease, before entering the evaporator.
    Inside the evaporator, the refrigerant absorbs heat from the refrigerated space
    and evaporates, after which the vapour returns to the compressor to repeat the
    cycle. Refrigerators are widely used in homes, commercial food storage, laboratories,
    and industrial cooling systems. From an engineering perspective, coefficient
    of performance, refrigerant properties, compressor efficiency, heat transfer,
    insulation, pressure losses, frost formation, and energy consumption are important
    factors affecting refrigeration performance.
  engineCategory: Engineering
